Question 3
As a student, I want to reserve an available study room for a particular time so that my group has a place to meet.

Use case: reserve an available study room

primary actor: the Student that wants to reserve the study room

preconditions:
The student is signed in
The student has already selected a room, date, and time
The room has no reservations currently

trigger:
The user asks the system to reserve the selected room

sucess outcomes:
The request is recorded as complete, reserving the room so that other students can not book it

main success scenario:
The student books a room on the system
The system checks if the room has been reserved already
The system records that the student has booked this room
The system notifies the student that the room is booked by them successfully
The system notifies other students that the room is booked

extension
2a The room was booked already by another student
i The system explains that the room was already booked
ii The system displays alternative available rooms or time slots, prompting the student to select an alternative
iii The Student may select to the alternative or quit, causing either the use case to continue with new input or ending
the use case

1a
i The student tries to book an invalid non-existing room
ii The system explains that no such room exist, and prompts the user to select an alternative room
iii The Student may select to the alternative or quit, causing either the use case to continue with new input or ending
the use case
What the user observes: An error message and a request to select an alternative room
State change: Depending on the user's choice, either a new room is booked or no state change happens.